  "p. 21 n. 1 (called after the ....Reχtet group, l. 16; out as words): \"The variants are\" [variant 1: a large oblique curved sign (plant/branch-like, unclear), two knotted-cord signs (as in the text, V12 approx), X1 above Z4, O49], [variant 2: two small cones over two Z11-like signs, D21, Aa1 (hatched disk) below, X1, X1, one knotted-cord sign over a Z11-like sign] \"(British Museum papyrus No. 9964) =\" [three cones over three Z11-like signs] [two lapwings G24 each on a basket V30] \"of Lepsius, Todtenbuch, Bl. L., l. 5. See Birch, Aeg. Zeitschrift, 1869, p. 115.\" The Lepsius variant (lapwings on baskets) suggests the cone-over-Z groups stand for rḫyt.",
  "p. 20 n. 1 (Or temṭu; see Brugsch...) belongs to àmṭu earlier on p. 20, outside this range."
