 "notes": "p. 20: only nuk / Ṭetṭeti / se after '13.' read. Words split by a line numeral (sebàu before/after '23.', segai before/after '26.', Seker before/after '29.', χebasi with its det after '30.') are given the line in which they begin. Budge's '....' (l. 16 before Reχtet, l. 17 twice) coded from the printed signs. Small x marks: on the horned viper I9 they are the viper's horns (not separate); in seś (l. 20) and śeta (l. 26) a free x Z9 inside the word; in the Seker bark det the x is part of the picture. Rubric overline only on p. 22 last row, over setekeni and baiu (starts just after à). The owl in this fount occurs in two shapes: with face (G17) and with open U-shaped head (coded G17 approx)."
